WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
- [Announcer] Please
put your hands together

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.280
for Danielle Perez. (audience cheers)

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.236
- You guys, keep it going
for those strong gentlemen.

00:00:07.236 --> 00:00:08.415
Keep it going for them.

00:00:08.415 --> 00:00:10.308
Lifting me on stage.

00:00:10.308 --> 00:00:12.244
I'm gonna hit them up
for a foot massage later.

00:00:12.244 --> 00:00:13.077
It's gonna be tight.

00:00:13.077 --> 00:00:15.912
When I'm on stage, and I'm performing,

00:00:15.912 --> 00:00:17.880
I feel really powerful.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.598
What I'm saying is being telegraphed

00:00:19.598 --> 00:00:21.209
to all these people that are there

00:00:21.209 --> 00:00:23.785
to hear my story and be exposed

00:00:23.785 --> 00:00:27.702
to, you know, a Latina who's disabled
and in a wheelchair.

00:00:28.558 --> 00:00:30.408
It's just a really important thing

00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:32.383
to be on stage representing that.

00:00:32.383 --> 00:00:36.133
(instrumental hip hop music)

00:00:37.685 --> 00:00:39.076
My name is Danielle Perez,

00:00:39.076 --> 00:00:41.064
and I'm a stand-up comedian.

00:00:41.064 --> 00:00:42.246
Performing stand-up comedy while

00:00:42.246 --> 00:00:45.943
using a wheelchair is
a bit of a challenge.

00:00:45.943 --> 00:00:48.166
First of all, people are always a little,

00:00:48.166 --> 00:00:49.316
they're just thrown off.

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:51.334
They don't really get
what's going on. (giggles)

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.890
I'm really excited to be here tonight,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.544
just debuting my new look,

00:00:54.544 --> 00:00:57.521
which is aggressively fat,
yet still very judge-y.

00:00:57.521 --> 00:00:59.205
(audience laughs)

00:00:59.205 --> 00:01:01.283
I started comedy three years ago.

00:01:01.283 --> 00:01:03.188
I realized I loved doing comedy

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:05.412
after my first open mic.

00:01:05.412 --> 00:01:09.251
People laughed at me,
and that felt so good.

00:01:09.251 --> 00:01:12.839
Like, I wanted to hold on to
that feeling forever,

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.751
and I was like, "I need
to do more of this."

00:01:14.751 --> 00:01:15.861
I'm a big girl, but I can tell

00:01:15.861 --> 00:01:17.251
that I've gained a little bit of weight

00:01:17.251 --> 00:01:18.211
because people keep asking me

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.496
if I have diabetes, which is really rude

00:01:20.496 --> 00:01:24.604
because I was hit by a
train. (audience laughs)

00:01:24.604 --> 00:01:26.994
I've gone through a lot of dark things.

00:01:26.994 --> 00:01:29.322
Eating disorders, depression,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.451
I lost my feet when I was 20.

00:01:32.451 --> 00:01:36.618
I definitely use comedy to
speak about those things,

00:01:37.698 --> 00:01:41.496
but also to entertain, and through that,

00:01:41.496 --> 00:01:43.346
find healing in myself.

00:01:43.346 --> 00:01:47.107
(contemplative piano music)

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:50.361
I think that comedy is really helpful tool

00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:53.549
in healing and bringing people together.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:56.820
When you see someone on stage that is

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:59.474
sharing a story or telling a joke,

00:01:59.474 --> 00:02:00.745
and you're like, "Oh, I get that.

00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:03.936
"I do that, too," it unifies and it brings

00:02:03.936 --> 00:02:06.750
people together, and
it's a form of catharsis.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.881
I ghosted on my therapist
about two years ago

00:02:08.881 --> 00:02:10.513
but realized I should get back into it

00:02:10.513 --> 00:02:12.602
when I started daydreaming
about walking into traffic,

00:02:12.602 --> 00:02:15.428
and I don't have feet. (audience laughs)

00:02:15.428 --> 00:02:16.947
I think the message that I want to put out

00:02:16.947 --> 00:02:19.043
in the world is that
it's okay to be yourself.

00:02:19.043 --> 00:02:22.801
It's okay to be weird and different.

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:25.712
You're only given one
opportunity in this world.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.966
So, make it the best you can.

00:02:27.966 --> 00:02:31.716
(instrumental hip hop music)

